laurel 2914: touch at the controller's rate. Finger down the TLMM latch is read every 2 ms and the panel on an edge; no edge for 20 ms (8 ms if none came yet): read anyway. One finger reads 16 bytes of I2C instead of 63, a long read sleeps 1 ms instead of 2. Before: a read every 12 ms, 8.4 ms late on average. New line LAUREL TOUCH RATE at the lift (at most one in 10 s): edges a second = the controller's real rate. Register 0x88 is only read. docs/laurel_sprout/gpu.md "Frame budget".

